      <room>K.3.401</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Color Management in SVG2</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>X.org+OpenICC Devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;SVG 1.1 is now widely implemented, and has some (minimal, optional) support for ICC colours. In the main though it is an sRGB system. SVG2 adds a conformance class for full ICC support (v2 and v4) including named colours, direct specification in LAB or LCHab, and interpolation in LAB or LCHab. Unmanaged device-specific colour is also supported.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description></description>
      <persons>
          <person id="3671">Chris Lilley</person>
      </persons>
      <links>
          <link href="http://www.w3c.org/">W3C</link>
      </links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>